 succeeded in 0ms:
   120	- Sell fill, no open trade: bootstrap a trade first (as above, quantity from the fill), then apply the exit. `needs_review: true`.
   121	- Every fill is a leg (`entry` or `exit`). Running quantity, `avg_entry`, `avg_exit`, `peak_quantity` recomputed.
   122	- Running quantity reaches zero: `status: closed`, `closed_at`, `realized_pnl` = exits − entries − commissions − fees + income legs.
   123	- `initial_risk` = quantity of the first entry leg × (its price − `planned_stop`), fixed at that moment. `realized_r` = `realized_pnl` / `initial_risk`, nil when no planned stop.
   124	- Cash dividend or interest with a CUSIP matching an open trade: `income` leg, feeds `realized_pnl`, does not touch basis.
   125	- Split or reverse split: `adjustment` leg with `ratio`, zero cash; `quantity`, `avg_entry`, `planned_stop`, `planned_target` scaled by the ratio.
   126	- Return of capital / basis change: `adjustment` leg with `cash_amount`, adjusts `avg_entry`.
   127	- CUSIP succession (merger, spin-off, reverse split issuing a new CUSIP): when an `out` on instrument A and an `in` on instrument B arrive as one corporate-action activity or within the same activity group, set `instruments.predecessor_instrument_id` on B and move the open trade to B with an `adjustment` leg. Unmatched halves fall back to normal exit/entry handling with `needs_review`.
   128	- Symbol change on a known CUSIP: update `instruments.symbol`, append `symbol_history`, trades untouched.
   129	- Idempotent via the unique index on `trade_legs.activity_id`, and one open trade per account and instrument via a partial unique index.
   130	
   131	**Review path** (Flow 4 plus the Monarch-style orphan review from the flows doc): trades with `needs_review` show a "N trades need review" banner on the dashboard. The review form takes setup, planned stop, and thesis; saving clears `needs_review`, computes `initial_risk`, and audits `trade_reviewed`. The post-mortem form (one line plus followed/improvised) is separate and available on any closed trade.
   132	
   133	---
   134	
   135	## 5. Stops and open risk in Phase 1
   136	
   137	No stop is not zero risk. `Sync::OrdersJob` identifies, per position, a working broker-side stop: a sell order on the same instrument with `order_type` STOP or STOP_LIMIT and status in the working set (WORKING, ACCEPTED, QUEUED, PENDING_ACTIVATION; enum unverified), following `replaces_order_id` chains. It sets `positions.working_stop_order_id` or clears it.
   138	
   139	- Protected position (a working stop order with a readable price): distance to stop = (last − stop) / last, signed; open risk = max(quantity × (last − stop), 0).
   140	- Unprotected position (no stop, a stop that is no longer working, or a trailing stop with no price): `unprotected` flag, distance and risk shown as unknown, never zero.
   141	- Portfolio open risk = sum over protected positions, and the dashboard and `get_account_health` state how many positions are excluded as unprotected.
   142	
   143	---
   144	
   145	## 6. Snapshots (per account, chain-linked)
   146	
   147	For each trading-enabled account and market day after close:
   148	- `equity` = latest balance equity for the day.
   149	- `net_flows` = sum of deposit and withdrawal transactions with `trade_date` on the day (deposits positive).
   150	- `daily_return` = (equity − net_flows − prior equity) / prior equity. First snapshot has return 0 and index 1.0.
   151	- `index_value` = prior index × (1 + daily_return); `high_water_index` = max to date; `drawdown_pct` = 1 − index / high_water_index.
   152	- `open_risk_amount`, `open_risk_pct`, `unprotected_count` from §5 at snapshot time.
   153	- Rebuildable: `Snapshots::RebuildJob(account, from:)` recomputes forward from any date, and `Sync::ActivitiesJob` enqueues a rebuild from the earliest newly seen deposit/withdrawal date, so a flow that lands a day late corrects the series.
   154	
   155	---
   156	
   157	## 7. UI (Hotwire, mobile-responsive, no JS routers, no hover-dependent modals)
   158	
   159	| Screen | Route | Phase 1 content |
   160	|---|---|---|
   161	| Dashboard | `/` | Banner (healthy / expiring / expired / halted), equity + day change, open risk with unprotected count, settled/unsettled cash, positions list with distance-to-stop as the primary number and inline `unprotected` where applicable, "N trades need review" callout, pending proposals count (0), staleness stamps on every number, empty state before first sync |
   162	| Trade review | `/trades/:id/review` | Setup, planned stop, thesis for `needs_review` trades; "N more to review" progression |
   163	| Trade detail / post-mortem | `/trades`, `/trades/:id` | List and detail; Flow 4 quick entry (one line + followed/improvised) |
   164	| System health | `/system` | Token age vs 7d with next Sunday marked, last sync per feed, sync pause reason, job failures (7d), API spend (month, from `agent_runs`), shadow mode indicator, manual halt toggle with reason (audited) |
   165	| Re-auth | `/schwab/authorize` → Schwab → `/schwab/callback` | Requires login; success page with new expiry and catch-up sync enqueued; failure page with error and retry |
   166	| Login | `/session/new` → email → `/session/magic/:token` | Passwordless; unknown emails get the same "check your inbox" response |
   167	
   168	**App mark:** the Athayde (Ataíde) family arms, azure, four bends argent running top-left to bottom-right, from the Portuguese Ataíde family (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ata%C3%ADde_family); the crest animal is a lion, reserved for later use. It sits top-left of the shell on every screen and serves as favicon and PWA icon. Vector at `app/assets/images/brand/crest.svg`, drawn from the athayde.com reference PNG kept in `docs/artifacts/brand/`.
   169	
   170	Banner precedence: halted > expired > expiring > healthy. Halted in Phase 1 comes only from `system_settings.manual_halt`.
   171	
   172	---
   173	
   174	## 8. Testing
   175	
   176	- **RSpec**, in the kickoff's priority order: token lifecycle with `travel_to` (25-minute refresh, 7-day expiry unaffected by refreshes, pause and catch-up, Mon/Tue escalation rule); sync jobs with fixture payloads (positions incl. removal, orders incl. cancel/replace and working stops, transactions incl. cash dividend, split, return of capital, CUSIP succession, fee items); journal linking (scale-in/out, orphan fill, sell-first legacy holding, bootstrap, ticker change on same CUSIP, R math); snapshot math (flows, late-landing deposit rebuild); MCP tool contracts (auth, each tool's schema and output, permission metadata excludes non-scheduled tools); scheduled runtime with a stubbed Messages API (turn cap, degraded mode).
   177	- **VCR cassettes** in `spec/cassettes`, recorded against Schwab only once the app is Ready For Use, with a scrubber that replaces bearer tokens, refresh tokens, and account hash values before write. Until then, cassettes are hand-built from community-client response shapes and marked `# SCHWAB_SHAPE_UNVERIFIED`.
   178	- **`Schwab::FakeClient`** implements the same interface as `Schwab::Client`, returns canned payloads, selected by `config.x.schwab.adapter`. Used by dev seeds and Playwright.
   179	- **Playwright** (`e2e/`, `@playwright/test` via npm, the only Node dependency): dashboard in four banner states via a test-env-only `/playwright/scenarios/:name` reseed route, MCP 401 page, re-auth success and failure (FakeClient scripted), trade review flow.
   180	- **`bin/ci`**: Rails 8.1 `ActiveSupport::ContinuousIntegration` with steps in `config/ci.rb`, the pattern borrowed from Patchvault. Kickoff order: rubocop → rspec → brakeman (strict, warnings fail) → `bin/importmap audit` → `bundle exec bundle-audit check --update` → Playwright (`bin/playwright`, which boots a test-env server with the FakeClient, runs `npx playwright test`, and tears down). Fails on the first red step.
   181	
   182	---
   183	
   184	## 9. Deploy
   185	
   186	- `Procfile`: `web: bundle exec puma -C config/puma.rb`, `worker: bin/jobs`, `release: bin/rails db:prepare`. Postgres service on the `postgres:17` image (structure.sql uses PG17 settings).
   187	- `app.json` for the release phase.
   188	- `bin/dokku-setup`: documents postgres plugin, letsencrypt, config vars (`RAILS_MASTER_KEY`, `SCHWAB_CALLBACK_URL`, `MEMORY_REPO_PATH`), storage mount for the memory repo, `ps:scale worker=1`, and the daily offsite DB dump from PRD §5.9 (postgres plugin backup to object storage on a cron).
   189	- App time zone `Eastern Time (US & Canada)`; Solid Queue recurring schedules use the same.
   190	
   191	---
   192	
   193	## 10. Build order (green `bin/ci` at each step)
   194	
   195	1. Tooling: RSpec, rubocop config, brakeman, bundler-audit, `bin/ci` (without Playwright), authentication generator adapted to magic link, AR encryption keys, credentials layout, crest in the layout.
   196	2. Migrations 1–21, models with validations/enums, `AuditEvent` append-only trigger, `SystemSettings` singleton.
   197	3. Schwab adapter: `Schwab::Client` (OAuth, accounts, positions, orders, transactions, market hours, quotes, price history) with retry/backoff/limiter, `Schwab::FakeClient`, response mappers, `docs/verify-on-approval.md` started from §12.
   198	4. OAuth controller + token model + refresh job + token health job + re-auth pages + pause/catch-up + audit events.
   199	5. Sync jobs, market calendar, tick scheduler, `sync_runs`, working-stop detection.
   200	6. Journal builder (bootstrap, link, review path) + setup stats + snapshots.
   201	7. Dashboard, system health, trade screens; Playwright added to `bin/ci`.
   202	8. MCP server + tool registry with permission metadata (after decision 0.8 is verified).
   203	9. Scheduled runtime + mailers (briefs, nags, failure digest) + memory repo pull.
   204	10. Seeds for dev via FakeClient; `Procfile`, `app.json`, `bin/dokku-setup`; DHH-skill review pass.
   205	
   206	---
   207	
   208	## 11. Explicitly not built in Phase 1
   209	
   210	Guardrail engine, order proposals (tables only), approval UI, submission, brackets, reconciliation job, allocation module, FMP, earnings/econ calendar, watchlist screen (watchlist.md in the memory repo is read as text), push notifications, iOS shell.
   211	
   212	---
   213	
   214	## 12. Schwab assumptions to verify on approval
   215	
   216	Maintained in `docs/verify-on-approval.md` (30 items as of the step 3 contract review). The original seed list:
   217	
   218	From PRD §9: exact `TaxLotMethod` enum values; order-endpoint rate limits. Added by this plan:
   219	- `/accounts/{hash}?fields=positions` returns balances in the same payload (`currentBalances`, `initialBalances`).
   220	- Which balance fields map to settled cash vs unsettled cash for a cash account.

