    69	
    70	`instrument.assetType`: EQUITY, OPTION, MUTUAL_FUND, CASH_EQUIVALENT, FIXED_INCOME, INDEX, CURRENCY, COLLECTIVE_INVESTMENT, FUTURE, FOREX, PRODUCT. The accounts API says EQUITY for ETFs where the quotes API says ETF; `instruments.asset_type` comes from the Trader API only. `cusip` and `instrumentId` are optional; cash equivalents and options often lack a CUSIP.
    71	
    72	Cash-account `currentBalances`: `cashAvailableForTrading`, `cashAvailableForWithdrawal`, `cashCall`, `longNonMarginableMarketValue`, `totalCash`, `cashDebitCallValue`, `unsettledCash`, `accruedInterest`, `cashBalance`, `cashReceipts`, `longOptionMarketValue`, `liquidationValue`, `longMarketValue`, `moneyMarketFund`, `savings`, `shortMarketValue`, `pendingDeposits`, `mutualFundValue`, `bondValue`, `shortOptionMarketValue`.
    73	
    74	Balance mapping: `equity` = `liquidationValue`; `cash_available_for_trading`; `unsettled_cash`; `cash_available_for_withdrawal`; `buying_power` nil for CASH. **`settled_cash` is derived, not a Schwab field.** Reading A: `cashAvailableForTrading - unsettledCash`. Reading B: `cashAvailableForWithdrawal`. Conservative: `min(A, B)` when both present. One named method, one spec per reading; Phase 2 guardrail 4 reads it.
    75	
    76	### `GET /accounts/{hash}/orders?fromEnteredTime=&toEnteredTime=&maxResults=3000[&status=]`
    77	`fromEnteredTime` and `toEnteredTime` are required together, `.SSSZ` UTC. Lookback is 60 days (schwab-py) or one year (Schwabdev); use 60 as one constant. `status` takes one enum value. `maxResults` default and max 3000; send it.
    78	
    79	**Also `GET /accounts/{hash}/orders/{orderId}`** for one order. Known working stops older than the lookback are re-fetched by id, otherwise positions get falsely flagged unprotected.
    80	
    81	```
    82	{ "orderId": <int64>, "accountNumber": <scrubbed>, "status", "statusDescription",
    83	  "orderType": MARKET|LIMIT|STOP|STOP_LIMIT|TRAILING_STOP|TRAILING_STOP_LIMIT|MARKET_ON_CLOSE|LIMIT_ON_CLOSE|CABINET|NON_MARKETABLE|EXERCISE|NET_DEBIT|NET_CREDIT|NET_ZERO|UNKNOWN,
    84	  "session": NORMAL|AM|PM|SEAMLESS, "duration": DAY|GOOD_TILL_CANCEL|FILL_OR_KILL|IMMEDIATE_OR_CANCEL|END_OF_WEEK|END_OF_MONTH|NEXT_END_OF_MONTH|UNKNOWN,
    85	  "orderStrategyType": SINGLE|OCO|TRIGGER|CANCEL|RECALL|PAIR|FLATTEN|TWO_DAY_SWAP|BLAST_ALL,
    86	  "quantity", "filledQuantity", "remainingQuantity", "price", "stopPrice", "stopType", "activationPrice",
    87	  "taxLotMethod": FIFO|LIFO|HIGH_COST|LOW_COST|AVERAGE_COST|SPECIFIC_LOT|LOSS_HARVESTER,
    88	  "enteredTime": "2026-08-14T13:31:02+0000", "closeTime", "cancelTime", "releaseTime", "cancelable", "editable", "tag",
    89	  "orderLegCollection": [ { "legId", "orderLegType", "instruction": BUY|SELL|BUY_TO_COVER|SELL_SHORT|BUY_TO_OPEN|BUY_TO_CLOSE|SELL_TO_OPEN|SELL_TO_CLOSE|EXCHANGE|SELL_SHORT_EXEMPT,
    90	                            "positionEffect": OPENING|CLOSING|AUTOMATIC, "quantity", "quantityType", "instrument": {...} } ],
    91	  "orderActivityCollection": [ { "activityType": EXECUTION|ORDER_ACTION, "executionType": "FILL", "quantity", "orderRemainingQuantity",
    92	                                 "executionLegs": [ { "legId", "price", "quantity", "mismarkedQuantity", "instrumentId", "time" } ] } ],
    93	  "childOrderStrategies": [ <full orders, recursive> ], "replacingOrderCollection": [ <full orders> ] }
    94	```
    95	
    96	Status enum: AWAITING_PARENT_ORDER, AWAITING_CONDITION, AWAITING_STOP_CONDITION, AWAITING_MANUAL_REVIEW, ACCEPTED, AWAITING_UR_OUT, PENDING_ACTIVATION, QUEUED, WORKING, REJECTED, PENDING_CANCEL, CANCELED (one L), PENDING_REPLACE, REPLACED, FILLED, EXPIRED, NEW, AWAITING_RELEASE_TIME, PENDING_ACKNOWLEDGEMENT, PENDING_RECALL, UNKNOWN.
    97	
    98	Working set for stop detection: WORKING, ACCEPTED, QUEUED, PENDING_ACTIVATION, AWAITING_PARENT_ORDER, AWAITING_STOP_CONDITION, AWAITING_CONDITION, NEW, AWAITING_RELEASE_TIME. A bracket child sits in AWAITING_PARENT_ORDER until the parent fills.
    99	
   100	Bracket children and replacements are **nested**, each a full order with its own `orderId`. The sync flattens recursively, setting `parent_order_id` and `replaces_order_id` as it walks.
   101	
   102	### `GET /accounts/{hash}/transactions?startDate=&endDate=[&types=][&symbol=]`
   103	`startDate`/`endDate` required together, `.SSSZ`, inclusive; a same-day query needs `endDate` at `23:59:59.000Z`. Lookback 60 days (same constant). `types` takes one value: TRADE, RECEIVE_AND_DELIVER, DIVIDEND_OR_INTEREST, ACH_RECEIPT, ACH_DISBURSEMENT, CASH_RECEIPT, CASH_DISBURSEMENT, ELECTRONIC_FUND, WIRE_OUT, WIRE_IN, JOURNAL, MEMORANDUM, MARGIN_CALL, MONEY_MARKET, SMA_ADJUSTMENT. Whether omitting it returns everything is unverified; the client loops the types the sync cares about.
   104	
   105	```
   106	{ "activityId": <int64, upsert key>, "time": "2026-08-14T13:31:02+0000", "user": {...drop...}, "description", "accountNumber": <scrubbed>,
   107	  "type", "status": VALID|INVALID|PENDING|UNKNOWN, "subAccount": CASH|MARGIN|SHORT|DIV|INCOME|UNKNOWN,
   108	  "tradeDate": "2026-08-14T00:00:00+0000", "settlementDate", "positionId", "orderId"?, "netAmount": <signed cash impact>,
   109	  "activityType": EXECUTION|ORDER_ACTION|TRANSFER|ACTIVITY_CORRECTION|UNKNOWN,
   110	  "transferItems": [ { "instrument": { "assetType":"EQUITY","cusip","symbol","instrumentId" }, "amount": <shares>, "cost", "price", "positionEffect" },
   111	                     { "instrument": { "assetType":"CURRENCY","symbol":"CURRENCY_USD" }, "amount": <dollars>, "feeType": "SEC_FEE" } ] }
   112	```
   113	
   114	The security item is the one without `feeType` whose instrument is not CURRENCY; its `amount` is share quantity. Fee items carry `feeType` (COMMISSION, SEC_FEE, STR_FEE, R_FEE, CDSC_FEE, OPT_REG_FEE, ADDITIONAL_FEE, MISCELLANEOUS_FEE, FUTURES_EXCHANGE_FEE, LOW_PROCEEDS_COMMISSION, BASE_CHARGE, GENERAL_CHARGE, GST_FEE, TAF_FEE, INDEX_OPTION_FEE, UNKNOWN) and `amount` in dollars. Side is derived from `positionEffect` plus the sign of `netAmount`; fees are the sum of `feeType` items, never from `cost`. `orderId` is present on TRADE executions only. Sign conventions and every corporate-action shape are unverified; RECEIVE_AND_DELIVER is the type for splits and CUSIP successions.
   115	
   116	## Market Data API
   117	
   118	### `GET /marketdata/v1/markets?markets=equity,option&date=YYYY-MM-DD`
   119	One date per call, today to one year out. Open day: `{"equity":{"EQ":{"date","marketType","product","isOpen":true,"sessionHours":{"preMarket":[{"start","end"}],"regularMarket":[...],"postMarket":[...]}}}}` with `-04:00` offsets. Closed day (TD-era behavior, unverified): key changes from `EQ` to `equity`, `sessionHours` absent, `isOpen` false. The mapper takes the first value under `equity` regardless of key, treats missing `sessionHours` as closed, and uses min start and max end per session. Early closes show as a shorter `regularMarket` interval.
   120	
   121	### `GET /marketdata/v1/quotes?symbols=A,B&fields=quote,reference&indicative=false`
   122	Symbols comma-joined and URL-encoded; chunk at 100. Response keyed by symbol: `assetMainType` (EQUITY|ETF|...), `assetSubType`, `quoteType`, `realtime`, `ssid`, `symbol`, `reference` {cusip, description, exchange, exchangeName}, `quote` {askPrice, bidPrice, lastPrice, mark, netChange, netPercentChange, openPrice, highPrice, lowPrice, closePrice, totalVolume, quoteTime, tradeTime, securityStatus, 52WeekHigh, 52WeekLow}, `regular` {regularMarketLastPrice, ...}. `quoteTime`/`tradeTime` are epoch ms. Unknown symbols return in the same 200 under a top-level `errors` key (`{"errors":{"invalidSymbols":[...]}}`); the mapper skips it and reports the list.
   123	
   124	### `GET /marketdata/v1/pricehistory?symbol=&periodType=&period=&frequencyType=&frequency=[&startDate=&endDate=]&needExtendedHoursData=false&needPreviousClose=true`
   125	`startDate`/`endDate` are epoch ms and override `period`. Valid combinations: day (1,2,3,4,5,10) with minute (1,5,10,15,30); month (1,2,3,6) with daily or weekly; year (1,2,3,5,10,15,20) with daily, weekly, monthly; ytd (1) with daily or weekly. Response `{"candles":[{"open","high","low","close","volume","datetime":<epoch ms>}],"symbol","empty","previousClose","previousCloseDate"}`. Daily `datetime` is midnight Eastern in UTC ms: convert in America/New_York. For the collar engine: `periodType=month&period=3&frequencyType=daily`.
   126	
   127	### `GET /marketdata/v1/instruments?symbol=&projection=symbol-search` and `GET /marketdata/v1/instruments/{cusip}`
   128	`{"instruments":[{"cusip","symbol","description","exchange","assetType"}]}`. The fallback for a position or transaction that arrives without a CUSIP. Preserve leading zeros.
   129	
   130	## Limits
   131	
   132	| Limit | Value used | Notes |
   133	|---|---|---|
   134	| Orders and transactions lookback | 60 days, one constant | Schwabdev says one year; probe 61+ days on approval |
   135	| Read rate limit | 100/min shared budget | community says 120/min per app, all APIs; unverified |
   136	| 429 handling | back off 1, 4, 16 s with jitter; `Retry-After` capped at 60 s | `Retry-After` presence unverified |
   137	| Quotes per call | 100 symbols | undocumented |
   138	| `maxResults` | 3000, sent explicitly | |
   139	| Market hours | one date per call, today to +1 year | |
   140	| Order write limit (Phase 2) | 120/min, 4000/day | QuantConnect figure |
   141	
   142	## FakeClient
   143	
   144	`Schwab::FakeClient` sits **below the mappers**: it returns scrubbed raw hashes in the same shape as the HTTP client, so seeds and Playwright exercise the mapping code where every shape assumption lives, and its fixtures double as the cassette-shaped fixtures for specs. It scripts auth too (`authorize_url`, `exchange_code`, `refresh`) and supports a per-call response queue so a test can say "first `orders` call raises RateLimited, second succeeds". Scenarios: re-auth success and failure, refresh expired, rate limited then success, server error then success, transport timeout, empty account, position removed between syncs, nested bracket child, transaction with missing CUSIP, unknown enum value, closed market day, quotes batch with one invalid symbol, and the four dashboard banner states.

