   214	## 12. Schwab assumptions to verify on approval
   215	
   216	Maintained in `docs/verify-on-approval.md` (30 items as of the step 3 contract review). The original seed list:
   217	
   218	From PRD §9: exact `TaxLotMethod` enum values; order-endpoint rate limits. Added by this plan:
   219	- `/accounts/{hash}?fields=positions` returns balances in the same payload (`currentBalances`, `initialBalances`).
   220	- Which balance fields map to settled cash vs unsettled cash for a cash account.
   221	- Orders endpoint supports `fromEnteredTime`/`toEnteredTime` and a `status` filter; maximum lookback window.
   222	- Transactions endpoint: 60-day start-date limit, `activityId` uniqueness, `orderId` presence on trade activities, transfer-item structure with fee items, CUSIP presence on every instrument (cash equivalents, sweeps, options).
   223	- Corporate-action activity shapes for splits, mergers, spin-offs, return of capital, and whether old and new CUSIPs arrive in one activity.
   224	- Market-hours endpoint takes one date per call and returns pre/regular/post session times.
   225	- Order status enum values for "working" stops; cancel/replace produces a new order id and marks the old one REPLACED.
   226	- Fractional-share quantities in positions and orders.
   227	- Refresh token expiry is 7 days from issuance and is not extended by access-token refreshes.
   228	- Claude app custom connectors: static bearer header availability for this org (decision 0.8).
   229	
   230	---
   231	
   232	## 13. Working method, per phase and per build step
   233	
   234	Each numbered step in §10 that ships a feature runs this loop:
   235	
   236	1. **PRD review with counselors** (`counselors run`, agents `codex-5.5-high` and `claude-fable`): the relevant PRD sections plus this plan's section for the step. Findings are folded into the plan before code.
   237	2. **Build** the feature vertically per §10.
   238	3. **RSpec green** and reviewed for coverage against the §8 priority list, not just passing.
   239	4. **DHH skill review pass** (`dhh-code-reviewer` agent) on the step's diff; fix what it flags.
   240	5. **Counselors review of the build** (same two agents) on the diff; fix or explicitly decline each finding in the commit message.
   241	6. **`bin/ci` green.** Commit.
   242	
   243	Counselors runs are long (10 to 20 minutes) and run in the background while unrelated work continues. Whole-phase gates: the counselors PRD review before step 1 (done, revision 2 of this plan is the result), and a DHH pass plus counselors review over the full Phase 1 diff after step 10.

